      "side": 1,
      "message": "You could also do something like this to avoid some needless kzallocs:\n```\n   buffer \u003d binder_alloc_new_buf_locked(alloc, NULL, size, is_async);\n   if (PTR_ERR(buffer) \u003d\u003d -ENOMEM) {\n     next \u003d kzalloc(...);\n     if (!next)\n       return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);\n    buffer \u003d binder_alloc_new_buf_locked(alloc, next, size, is_async);\n```\ninstead of proactive allocation at line 549.\n\nThis would mean bailing out of `binder_alloc_new_buffer_locked()` as soon as you see `size \u003c buffer_size`.\n\nPerhaps this is overkill given the new buffer is actually used 98% of the time, so feel free to ignore - which I guess makes sense since we tend to coalesce with adjacent buffers when we free.",
